Don Galt[050717][050717][050717]Hey--<BR><BR>The whole care sales thing is a scam. Especially if you're buying a new care.  I strongly recommend you read "Don't get taken every time" by Remar Sutton.  And spend the $30 to get a report on the vehicle you want from fighting chance www.fightingchance.com.<BR><BR>One of the key pieces of information is how much the vehicle actually cost the dealer, without that you're negotiating in a vacuum.  You can get this from fighting chance.  You won't ever get it from a dealer. <BR><BR>Also, the last week of the month is a good time to buy.  The dealers are more desperate then.  The last week of the year, or christmas week is fantastic- end of the year inventory and no buyers, means great deals.<BR><BR>When I bought mine recently, I test drove at a time I couldn't buy, and determined what I wanted.  After the test drive, I did not set foot on a dealers lot again until I picked up the vehicle I bought.<BR><BR>I got the fax number for every toyota dealership in the state.  I sent them an offer letter.  I told them in the offer letter the exact vehicle I wanted to buy, and how much it would cost with $500 profit.  I asked them to fax written offers to me, and I got about 23 offers.<BR><BR>I would have done better if I'd found the options configuration that was exactly like what the factory made... they tend to do configurations of options rather than each option individually... so I'd check that out before deciding what you want- you can find this out on dealer websites looking at the combination of optiosn they offer,... the standard configuration will become obvious.<BR><BR>Anyway, long story short, I saved about %15...I got a better deal than anybody walking onto a lot ever will.  And I did it all from my home.   I gave them my email and phone number in the fax, that was a mistake-- they tried to pitch me over the phone... I'd recommend giving them only the options of email and fax for written offers.<BR><BR>Lots more advice I can give but this is getting long... Good luck and have fun![050717]07-17-2005 18:10
